# Environment Variables

## Schema Definition

Define env schemas in `src/lib/server/env.server.ts`:

```typescript
import { z } from 'zod';

const PrivateEnvSchema = z.object({
  AZURE_CS_CONNECTION_STRING: z.string(),
  SOME_OPTIONAL_VAR: z.string().optional(),
  VAR_WITH_DEFAULT: z.string().default('default-value')
});

const PublicEnvSchema = z.object({
  PUBLIC_API_URL: z.url().default('http://localhost:5173')
});
```

## Adding New Variables

1. Add to schema in `env.server.ts`
2. Add to `.env.example` with example/placeholder value
3. Use typed getter:

```typescript
import { PrivateEnvValue, PublicEnvValue } from '$lib/server';

// Private (server-only)
const connectionString = PrivateEnvValue('AZURE_CS_CONNECTION_STRING');

// Public (can be exposed to client)
const apiUrl = PublicEnvValue('PUBLIC_API_URL');
```

## Conventions

- Private vars: No prefix (server-only)
- Public vars: `PUBLIC_` prefix (SvelteKit convention)
- Azure vars: `AZURE_` prefix
- Always validate with Zod
- Provide sensible defaults where appropriate
